Under ADR-0057 §11 a tree-sitter `calls` edge to an external stub and a
SCIP `calls` edge resolved to a first-party item at the same site are two
edges (they disagree on dst), and until now the wrong answer sat at equal
standing with the right one. §14 (owner ruling 2026-09-18): the resolved
edge DEMOTES the stub, by rank_score, never deletes it, and records why.

Placement: finalize sub-step 7a, _finalize_demote_superseded_stubs, right
after the ADR-0037 resolution verdict — is_resolved is settled in Phase E,
so the merge pass could not know which edge is the stub. The stamp and
the rank adjustment both live here.

The measurement the row required changed its number. On the committed
aardvark-dns fixture 244 tree-sitter call edges end at a stub; 63 share a
(src, line) with some resolved edge; 27 with a resolved edge of the same
type; only 3 also name the same callee — every `wrap` the syntactic arm
left external and the SCIP arm resolved to `Result::wrap`. The other 24
are different calls that share a line (`a.b(c.d())`); demoting them would
have been the false supersession the row warned about, and 5 of the 27
were "superseded" only by the same producer's other call. So the rule as
landed requires all of: same src, a shared call line (call_lines-aware),
the same edge_type, the same declared callee name key (the language's
incumbent anchor applied to the resolved dst's name and the stub's
dst_ref.name / id name slot), and a producer in the resolved edge's origin
that the stub's origin lacks. Languages with one anchored producer are
untouched by construction.

The demotion: rank_score *= SUPERSEDED_STUB_RANK_FACTOR (0.5, declared —
the ADR-0039 ruling-3 multiplicative shape; joins WI-hukuf's table);
confidence untouched; nothing deleted; edge count unchanged.
meta.superseded_by / meta.superseded_by_origin — two new registered
edge-meta keys, docs/schema.json regenerated — name the superseding edge
and its producers, so a low rank is a stated fact.

Tests: 12 unit tests on synthetic two-producer edges (fires for another
producer's resolved call and for a merged edge, honours call_lines; does
not fire for a different callee, the same producer, a different line or
type, two stubs, a single-producer language; reads the callee from the id
when dst_ref is absent; takes rank_score from confidence when unset); the
fixture pins 244 stub calls, 3 superseded (each stamped with a SCIP-only
edge to Result::wrap), 24 co-located sites untouched, every other
rank_score and the edge count unchanged. Mutation: dropping the
callee-name condition turns the unit and fixture pins red. The finalize
sub-step order list gains the entry.

Slice: 475 affected test files in 12 foreground chunks plus the
schema-coverage file serially (WI-rukil), 18,340 passed; finalize.py and
axis_meta_keys.py coverage 100%; mypy ratchet 667 unchanged.

